{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788619764890,"sessionID":"ses_f8df4cef5ffeQvGnhv2x0LLXr4","part":{"id":"prt_0720bb498001Yr7Dn1Mu62NzZr","messageID":"msg_0720bb179001dNDsSmMR3WTJ60","sessionID":"ses_f8df4cef5ffeQvGnhv2x0LLXr4","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788619770835,"sessionID":"ses_f8df4cef5ffeQvGnhv2x0LLXr4","part":{"id":"prt_0720bb4990015xqFn1m4UX45Y8","messageID":"msg_0720bb179001dNDsSmMR3WTJ60","sessionID":"ses_f8df4cef5ffeQvGnhv2x0LLXr4","type":"text","text":"I now have a complete understanding. Let me produce the task breakdown.\n\n## Analysis Summary\n\n**Root cause:** In `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, the \"Add Note\" button in the category detail header (line 118) calls `notes.openModal('note')` without setting `notes.createParent`. The current category is tracked only in the component's local `stack`/`current` state, not in the shared `NotesSvelte` store. So `notes.create()` runs with `createParent === null`, creating the note in the root (no `category_id`).\n\n**Why it doesn't show up:** On mobile, once the nav drawer closes and the user views the overview or navigates within a category, root-level notes are not shown in the category the user was viewing, so the note appears \"not created\".\n\n**Fix direction:** Set `notes.createParent` to the currently-viewed category before opening the note modal from the mobile category detail header; and explicitly set it to `null` for the root-level AddNoteButton to avoid stale state from a prior category visit.\n\n**Testability note:** The fix is in a `.svelte` component, which the repo does not unit-test (only pure helpers/services/stores). The `create()` + `createParent` behavior in the store is already covered by `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`. No new unit test can directly cover the component wiring.\n\nThe branch per brief is `feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category`; the mounted worktree is on the job branch.\n\n---\n\n## Task List\n\n**TASK-1: Set the create parent category for the mobile \"Add Note\" button in a category detail view**\n- Description: In `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, make the \"Add Note\" button in the category detail header set `notes.createParent = current.id` before calling `notes.openModal('note')`, so a note created there lands in the currently-viewed category instead of the root.\n- Files: `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`\n- Depends: none\n- Risk: low — a small, isolated change to the mobile nav component; the store's `create()` already honors `createParent` and resets it after creation (covered by existing store tests).\n\n**TASK-2: Reset the create parent to root for the mobile root-level \"Add Note\" button**\n- Description: In `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, explicitly set `notes.createParent = null` on the root-level \"Add Note\" button (line 63) before opening the note modal, so a note created at the root always goes to root even if `createParent` is stale from a prior category visit.\n- Files: `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`\n- Depends: TASK-1 (same file; combine edits if convenient)\n- Risk: low — same component, explicit null assignment; prevents cross-contamination of stale state.\n\n**TASK-3 (optional hardening): Make `openModal('note')` default-safe against stale `createParent`**\n- Description: Consider clearing `createParent` in `NotesSvelte.openModal('note')` when no explicit parent is passed (and mirror for 'category'), so root-level \"Add Note\"/\"Add Folder\" buttons (mobile and desktop) can never accidentally inherit a stale parent set by a previous right-click/category interaction.\n- Files: `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`, `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`\n- Depends: none\n- Risk: medium — touches shared store logic used by the desktop right-click flow and category creation; requires care not to break existing `createParent` semantics and existing tests. Mark as optional since the brief scopes to the mobile bug; only do if the developer confirms it's needed to fully prevent stale-state regressions.\n\n---\n\nI'll present the task breakdown now. Since the primary fix (TASK-1 + TASK-2) directly resolves the brief with minimal risk, and TASK-3 is a broader hardening that touches shared store behavior beyond the mobile scope, I'll keep TASK-3 clearly optional to respect the \"be conservative / don't over-expand scope\" guidance.\n\nI should note that there is no clear blocker requiring human input; the scope is well-defined and I can proceed with the recommended task list.\n\nHere is the structured task list:\n\n**TASK-1 — Set the create parent category for the mobile \"Add Note\" button in a category detail view**\n- Description: Make the \"Add Note\" button in the mobile category detail header set `notes.createParent = current.id` before `notes.openModal('note')`, so notes created there land in the currently-viewed category instead of the root.\n- Files: `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`\n- Depends: none\n- Risk: low — small isolated change; `create()` already honors and resets `createParent`.\n\n**TASK-2 — Reset create parent to root for the mobile root-level \"Add Note\" button**\n- Description: Explicitly set `notes.createParent = null` on the root-level \"Add Note\" button before opening the note modal, preventing stale category state from a prior category visit.\n- Files: `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`\n- Depends: TASK-1\n- Risk: low — same component, explicit null assignment.\n\n**TASK-3 (optional) — Harden `openModal` against stale `createParent`**\n- Description: Clear `createParent` in `openModal('note'/'category')` when no parent is provided, so any root-level Add button can't inherit stale state from a prior right-click/category interaction.\n- Files: `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`, `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`\n- Depends: none\n- Risk: medium — touches shared store logic used by desktop right-click and category creation; needs care with existing tests. Optional; only if needed to fully prevent stale-state regressions.\n\nTASK-1 and TASK-2 directly and fully resolve the brief with low risk. I'll recommend the developer implement those two, and treat TASK-3 as optional hardening they can pick up if they want determinism across desktop/mobile Add buttons.","time":{"start":1788619764889,"end":1788619770832}}}
