{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788619790812,"sessionID":"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i","part":{"id":"prt_0720c198e001GdgZI1FDX384nX","messageID":"msg_0720c14690014xlTwj44MPanL5","sessionID":"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788619825373,"sessionID":"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_8789759288aa4290a555a54d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md","content":"# Tasks: mobile: note is created without category\n\nid: toy\nstatus: open\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-09-05\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\nTASK-1: Add an `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` method to the `NotesSvelte` store that sets `createParent = parent` and then calls the existing `openModal('note')`, following the same pattern as `openRightClickMenu`/`openModal` already on the store.\n     files: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — a thin store method that sets one existing field and delegates to an existing method; no changes to `create()` logic.\n\nTASK-2: Wire both mobile navigation \"Create Note\" buttons to the new store method so the created note lands in the currently-viewed category: the category-detail `AddNoteButton` (NoteNavigationMobile.svelte line 118) must open with `current.id`, and the root `AddNoteButton` (line 63) must open with `null` to avoid stale `createParent` leakage.\n     files: src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — targeted change to the two onClick handlers; the `current` derived value already holds the category being viewed.\n\nTASK-3: Add unit tests to `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` for `openCreateNoteModal` verifying it sets `createParent` to the passed parent (and that a `null` parent clears it) and opens the modal, so the wiring is covered by the existing store-test suite.\n     files: tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — follows the existing `create`/`createParent` test pattern in the same file.\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md","time":{"start":1788619825363,"end":1788619825372}},"id":"prt_0720c9fc8001uaT4GyX6NJVj9J","sessionID":"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i","messageID":"msg_0720c14690014xlTwj44MPanL5"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788619825496,"sessionID":"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i","part":{"id":"prt_0720c9fac001MVsR7k46w4HM36","messageID":"msg_0720c14690014xlTwj44MPanL5","sessionID":"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i","type":"text","text":"I now have a complete understanding of the bug. Let me confirm my branch understanding and the store test patterns, then produce the task breakdown.\n\nThe root cause is confirmed:\n\n- **`NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` line 118** — in the category detail view (`{:else}` branch), the `AddNoteButton` calls `notes.openModal('note')` directly, without setting `notes.createParent`. The store's `create()` (Notes.svelte.ts:194-227) uses `this.createParent` to decide `category_id`, so the note falls into the root (null parent).\n- The mobile nav tracks the currently-viewed category only in *local* component state (`stack`/`current`), never in the shared store.\n- **Root AddNoteButton (line 63)** also calls `openModal('note')` without resetting `createParent`, so a stale parent could leak into the root button after a cancelled create inside a category.\n- Desktop is unaffected: its per-category creation goes through the right-click menu (`openRightClickMenu` → sets `createParent`, Notes.svelte.ts:171), and the desktop `AddNoteButton` is a top-level notebook button.\n- The store's `create()` with `createParent` is already unit-tested (Notes.test.ts:205-217). The existing `openModal`/`openRightClickMenu` pattern lives on the store, so adding a store method is consistent and unit-testable (component wiring alone isn't covered by the Vitest setup).\n\nLet me record the task breakdown in `tasks.md`.\n\n","time":{"start":1788619825068,"end":1788619825491}}}
