{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620004061,"sessionID":"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_c9390b463afe42c0bac9736c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git diff docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log | head -20","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"diff --git a/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log b/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log\nindex 807b43b..a8643ea 100644\n--- a/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log\n+++ b/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log\n@@ -103,3 +103,103 @@\n {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1788619826616,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ca5b6001i8FdrFZIk4yCTT\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720ca1640018A8NL1vC5udkG1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1788619831877,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ca666001dQM2Bmhw9yBKbF\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720ca1640018A8NL1vC5udkG1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"## Analysis complete\\n\\nI read `brief.md` (branch `feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category`; the mounted worktree is this job's branch, so no checkout needed) and the notes feature source. The render-report `screenshots/` for this job is empty, so there is no rendered ground truth to consult — analysis is code-based.\\n\\n### Root cause\\nOn mobile, browsing into a category via `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` only tracks the viewed category in local component state (`stack`/`current`, lines 19–23). The category-detail **\\\"Create Note\\\"** button (line 118) calls `notes.openModal('note')` without setting the shared store's `createParent`, so `NotesSvelte.create()` (Notes.svelte.ts:194–227) sends no `category_id` and the note lands in the root. The root button (line 63) likewise never resets `createParent`, so a stale parent from a cancelled in-category create could leak. Desktop is unaffected — its per-category creation goes through the right-click menu, which sets `createParent` (Notes.svelte.ts:171).\\n\\n### Task breakdown\\n- **TASK-1** — Add `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` to `NotesSvelte` (sets `createParent` then calls `openModal('note')`), matching the existing `openModal`/`openRightClickMenu` store pattern. Files: `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`. Depends: none. Risk: low.\\n- **TASK-2** — Wire both mobile \\\"Create Note\\\" buttons in `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`: the category-detail button (line 118) opens with `current.id`; the root button (line 63) opens with `null` to prevent stale-parent leakage. Files: `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`. Depends: TASK-1. Risk: low.\\n- **TASK-3** — Add unit tests for `openCreateNoteModal` (sets/clears `createParent`, opens modal) in `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`, following the existing `create`/`createParent` test pattern. Depends: TASK-1. Risk: low.\\n\\nTasks recorded in `/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md`.\\n\\nNote on verification: the fix is component wiring in a `.svelte` file; the repo's Vitest suite covers stores/services only, so the store method (TASK-1) is the unit-testable seam — a rendered/manual check of the mobile nav flow would still be advisable at review time since no render report exists for this job.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619826790,\"end\":1788619831875}}}\n {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1788619831890,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cba4a001nSWB95AWUDftqD\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720ca1640018A8NL1vC5udkG1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":44493,\"input\":3749,\"output\":595,\"reasoning\":14,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":40135}},\"cost\":0.00181916}}\n+\n+=== 2026-09-05T16:50:32+02:00 developer (attempt 1) ===\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1788619836802,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ccd80001p77oJPU9SafrJ3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1788619837358,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_63119237de52421e98cdafda\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Brief: mobile: note is created without category\\n2: \\n3: status: open\\n4: type: feature\\n5: id: toy\\n6: branch: feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\n7: date: 2026-09-05\\n8: author: Leander Muskalla\\n9: \\n10: ## What\\n11: \\n12: If I use the mobile navigation to browse to a category and then hit the \\\"Create Note\\\" button there, it'll add the note but not in the category I'm currently looking at.\\n13: \\n14: ## Why\\n15: \\n16: The user expects the note to land where he's currently at.\\n17: Also, if it lands in the root, it'll not show up for the user at all, so it seems it was not created at all.\\n18: \\n19: ## Out of scope\\n20: \\n21: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n22: \\n23: ## Notes\\n24: \\n25: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\\n\\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\\n</content>\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\\n# solyto frontend\\n\\n<!--\\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \\\"the agent\\\", not for one vendor.\\n-->\\n\\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\\n\\n## Stack\\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\\n\\n## Commands\\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\\n\\n</system-reminder>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# Brief: mobile: note is created without category\\n\\nstatus: open\\ntype: feature\\nid: toy\\nbranch: feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\ndate: 2026-09-05\\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n\\n## What\\n\\nIf I use the mobile navigation to browse to a category and then hit the \\\"Create Note\\\" button there, it'll add the note but not in the category I'm currently looking at.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe user expects the note to land where he's currently at.\\nAlso, if it lands in the root, it'll not show up for the user at all, so it seems it was not created at all.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[\"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\"],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md\",\"text\":\"# Brief: mobile: note is created without category\\n\\nstatus: open\\ntype: feature\\nid: toy\\nbranch: feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\ndate: 2026-09-05\\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n\\n## What\\n\\nIf I use the mobile navigation to browse to a category and then hit the \\\"Create Note\\\" button there, it'll add the note but not in the category I'm currently looking at.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe user expects the note to land where he's currently at.\\nAlso, if it lands in the root, it'll not show up for the user at all, so it seems it was not created at all.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":25,\"totalLines\":25,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619837342,\"end\":1788619837356}},\"id\":\"prt_0720cce3f001MC9Ig4tgSG596D\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1788619838163,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_7197647a7299486d977677f7\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git branch --show-current\",\"workdir\":\"/workspace\"},\"output\":\"feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"git branch --show-current\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619838139,\"end\":1788619838162}},\"id\":\"prt_0720ccff8001fu5dO2T6SU7fCk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1788619838208,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ccd87001fJb7NNIhNFpxWt\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll start by reading the job's brief.md.\\n\\n\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619836807,\"end\":1788619838205}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1788619838221,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cd306001AfHoJpEaDT3kKQ\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":11833,\"input\":11705,\"output\":128,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0.00167454}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1788619839138,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cd69f001vCbEX4ZLKBrWHi\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cd30b001IyxoRp5SjHYCKZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1788619839617,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_0968d4eb8cc3490396cef1f1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Tasks: mobile: note is created without category\\n2: \\n3: id: toy\\n4: status: open\\n5: analyst: analyst\\n6: date: 2026-09-05\\n7: \\n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\\n9: \\n10: ## Task breakdown\\n11: \\n12: <!-- TASK-1: description\\n13:      files: list of files likely affected\\n14:      depends: none\\n15:      risk: low / medium / high — reason\\n16: \\n17: TASK-2: ...\\n18: -->\\n19: \\n20: TASK-1: Add an `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` method to the `NotesSvelte` store that sets `createParent = parent` and then calls the existing `openModal('note')`, following the same pattern as `openRightClickMenu`/`openModal` already on the store.\\n21:      files: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts\\n22:      depends: none\\n23:      risk: low — a thin store method that sets one existing field and delegates to an existing method; no changes to `create()` logic.\\n24: \\n25: TASK-2: Wire both mobile navigation \\\"Create Note\\\" buttons to the new store method so the created note lands in the currently-viewed category: the category-detail `AddNoteButton` (NoteNavigationMobile.svelte line 118) must open with `current.id`, and the root `AddNoteButton` (line 63) must open with `null` to avoid stale `createParent` leakage.\\n26:      files: src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte\\n27:      depends: TASK-1\\n28:      risk: low — targeted change to the two onClick handlers; the `current` derived value already holds the category being viewed.\\n29: \\n30: TASK-3: Add unit tests to `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` for `openCreateNoteModal` verifying it sets `createParent` to the passed parent (and that a `null` parent clears it) and opens the modal, so the wiring is covered by the existing store-test suite.\\n31:      files: tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts\\n32:      depends: TASK-1\\n33:      risk: low — follows the existing `create`/`createParent` test pattern in the same file.\\n\\n(End of file - total 33 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# Tasks: mobile: note is created without category\\n\\nid: toy\\nstatus: open\\nanalyst: analyst\\ndate: 2026-09-05\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\\n\\n## Task breakdown\\n\\n<!-- TASK-1: description\\n     files: list of files likely affected\\n     depends: none\\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\\n\\nTASK-2: ...\\n-->\\n\\nTASK-1: Add an `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` method to the `NotesSvelte` store that sets `createParent = parent` and then calls the existing `openModal('note')`, following the same pattern as `openRightClickMenu`/`openModal` already on the store.\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md\",\"text\":\"# Tasks: mobile: note is created without category\\n\\nid: toy\\nstatus: open\\nanalyst: analyst\\ndate: 2026-09-05\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\\n\\n## Task breakdown\\n\\n<!-- TASK-1: description\\n     files: list of files likely affected\\n     depends: none\\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\\n\\nTASK-2: ...\\n-->\\n\\nTASK-1: Add an `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` method to the `NotesSvelte` store that sets `createParent = parent` and then calls the existing `openModal('note')`, following the same pattern as `openRightClickMenu`/`openModal` already on the store.\\n     files: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts\\n     depends: none\\n     risk: low — a thin store method that sets one existing field and delegates to an existing method; no changes to `create()` logic.\\n\\nTASK-2: Wire both mobile navigation \\\"Create Note\\\" buttons to the new store method so the created note lands in the currently-viewed category: the category-detail `AddNoteButton` (NoteNavigationMobile.svelte line 118) must open with `current.id`, and the root `AddNoteButton` (line 63) must open with `null` to avoid stale `createParent` leakage.\\n     files: src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte\\n     depends: TASK-1\\n     risk: low — targeted change to the two onClick handlers; the `current` derived value already holds the category being viewed.\\n\\nTASK-3: Add unit tests to `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` for `openCreateNoteModal` verifying it sets `createParent` to the passed parent (and that a `null` parent clears it) and opens the modal, so the wiring is covered by the existing store-test suite.\\n     files: tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts\\n     depends: TASK-1\\n     risk: low — follows the existing `create`/`createParent` test pattern in the same file.\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":33,\"totalLines\":33,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619839607,\"end\":1788619839616}},\"id\":\"prt_0720cd7a4001XIIfE9Q4cHhAJa\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cd30b001IyxoRp5SjHYCKZ\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1788619839673,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cd722001grQe5B4rIml5l4\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cd30b001IyxoRp5SjHYCKZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The branch matches. Let me check the tasks.md file.\\n\\n\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619839266,\"end\":1788619839670}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1788619839688,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cd8c3001AHpnOa2lnTF5Dx\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cd30b001IyxoRp5SjHYCKZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":14238,\"input\":2445,\"output\":77,\"reasoning\":12,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":11704}},\"cost\":0.000694932}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1788619840702,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cdcbd001iyEQxCPw9CdB6V\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cd8c7001eAHdybYYAF0QNR\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n","metadata":{"output":"diff --git a/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log b/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log\nindex 807b43b..a8643ea 100644\n--- a/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log\n+++ b/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/session.log\n@@ -103,3 +103,103 @@\n {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1788619826616,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ca5b6001i8FdrFZIk4yCTT\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720ca1640018A8NL1vC5udkG1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1788619831877,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ca666001dQM2Bmhw9yBKbF\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720ca1640018A8NL1vC5udkG1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"## Analysis complete\\n\\nI read `brief.md` (branch `feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category`; the mounted worktree is this job's branch, so no checkout needed) and the notes feature source. The render-report `screenshots/` for this job is empty, so there is no rendered ground truth to consult — analysis is code-based.\\n\\n### Root cause\\nOn mobile, browsing into a category via `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` only tracks the viewed category in local component state (`stack`/`current`, lines 19–23). The category-detail **\\\"Create Note\\\"** button (line 118) calls `notes.openModal('note')` without setting the shared store's `createParent`, so `NotesSvelte.create()` (Notes.svelte.ts:194–227) sends no `category_id` and the note lands in the root. The root button (line 63) likewise never resets `createParent`, so a stale parent from a cancelled in-category create could leak. Desktop is unaffected — its per-category creation goes through the right-click menu, which sets `createParent` (Notes.svelte.ts:171).\\n\\n### Task breakdown\\n- **TASK-1** — Add `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` to `NotesSvelte` (sets `createParent` then calls `openModal('note')`), matching the existing `openModal`/`openRightClickMenu` store pattern. Files: `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`. Depends: none. Risk: low.\\n- **TASK-2** — Wire both mobile \\\"Create Note\\\" buttons in `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`: the category-detail button (line 118) opens with `current.id`; the root button (line 63) opens with `null` to prevent stale-parent leakage. Files: `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`. Depends: TASK-1. Risk: low.\\n- **TASK-3** — Add unit tests for `openCreateNoteModal` (sets/clears `createParent`, opens modal) in `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`, following the existing `create`/`createParent` test pattern. Depends: TASK-1. Risk: low.\\n\\nTasks recorded in `/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/tasks.md`.\\n\\nNote on verification: the fix is component wiring in a `.svelte` file; the repo's Vitest suite covers stores/services only, so the store method (TASK-1) is the unit-testable seam — a rendered/manual check of the mobile nav flow would still be advisable at review time since no render report exists for this job.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619826790,\"end\":1788619831875}}}\n {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1788619831890,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cba4a001nSWB95AWUDftqD\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720ca1640018A8NL1vC5udkG1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df42ffdffeMnfPr2offFS97i\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":44493,\"input\":3749,\"output\":595,\"reasoning\":14,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":40135}},\"cost\":0.00181916}}\n+\n+=== 2026-09-05T16:50:32+02:00 developer (attempt 1) ===\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1788619836802,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ccd80001p77oJPU9SafrJ3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1788619837358,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_63119237de52421e98cdafda\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Brief: mobile: note is created without category\\n2: \\n3: status: open\\n4: type: feature\\n5: id: toy\\n6: branch: feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\n7: date: 2026-09-05\\n8: author: Leander Muskalla\\n9: \\n10: ## What\\n11: \\n12: If I use the mobile navigation to browse to a category and then hit the \\\"Create Note\\\" button there, it'll add the note but not in the category I'm currently looking at.\\n13: \\n14: ## Why\\n15: \\n16: The user expects the note to land where he's currently at.\\n17: Also, if it lands in the root, it'll not show up for the user at all, so it seems it was not created at all.\\n18: \\n19: ## Out of scope\\n20: \\n21: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n22: \\n23: ## Notes\\n24: \\n25: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\\n\\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\\n</content>\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\\n# solyto frontend\\n\\n<!--\\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \\\"the agent\\\", not for one vendor.\\n-->\\n\\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\\n\\n## Stack\\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\\n\\n## Commands\\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\\n\\n</system-reminder>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# Brief: mobile: note is created without category\\n\\nstatus: open\\ntype: feature\\nid: toy\\nbranch: feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\ndate: 2026-09-05\\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n\\n## What\\n\\nIf I use the mobile navigation to browse to a category and then hit the \\\"Create Note\\\" button there, it'll add the note but not in the category I'm currently looking at.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe user expects the note to land where he's currently at.\\nAlso, if it lands in the root, it'll not show up for the user at all, so it seems it was not created at all.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[\"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\"],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md\",\"text\":\"# Brief: mobile: note is created without category\\n\\nstatus: open\\ntype: feature\\nid: toy\\nbranch: feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\ndate: 2026-09-05\\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n\\n## What\\n\\nIf I use the mobile navigation to browse to a category and then hit the \\\"Create Note\\\" button there, it'll add the note but not in the category I'm currently looking at.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nThe user expects the note to land where he's currently at.\\nAlso, if it lands in the root, it'll not show up for the user at all, so it seems it was not created at all.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":25,\"totalLines\":25,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category/brief.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619837342,\"end\":1788619837356}},\"id\":\"prt_0720cce3f001MC9Ig4tgSG596D\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1788619838163,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_7197647a7299486d977677f7\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git branch --show-current\",\"workdir\":\"/workspace\"},\"output\":\"feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"git branch --show-current\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619838139,\"end\":1788619838162}},\"id\":\"prt_0720ccff8001fu5dO2T6SU7fCk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1788619838208,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720ccd87001fJb7NNIhNFpxWt\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll start by reading the job's brief.md.\\n\\n\",\"time\":{\"start\":1788619836807,\"end\":1788619838205}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1788619838221,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0720cd306001AfHoJpEaDT3kKQ\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0720cc07c001jjPFoKSTanjd7Q\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":11833,\"input\":11705,\"output\":128,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0.00167454}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\