{"type":"text","timestamp":1788620140349,"sessionID":"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG","part":{"id":"prt_07211610c001LVmEjB7vADxUuj","messageID":"msg_072115e1d001M6W7ArfEdsXtEU","sessionID":"ses_f8df34085ffedgwCvVGAM3ECYG","type":"text","text":"The worktree is clean. All tasks are complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Job:** mobile: note is created without category (`feature/toy_mobile-note-is-created-without-category`)\n\n**Root cause:** On mobile, the category-detail \"Create Note\" button in `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` called `notes.openModal('note')` without setting the store's `createParent`, so `NotesSvelte.create()` sent no `category_id` and the note landed in the root (invisible to the user viewing a category).\n\n**Implemented:**\n\n- **TASK-1** (`src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`): Added `openCreateNoteModal(parent: number | null)` — sets `createParent = parent`, then delegates to the existing `openModal('note')`, matching the `openRightClickMenu`/`openModal` store pattern.\n- **TASK-2** (`src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`): Category-detail `AddNoteButton` now opens with `current.id` (the category being viewed); root `AddNoteButton` opens with `null` to prevent stale `createParent` leakage.\n- **TASK-3** (`tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`): Added 2 tests verifying `openCreateNoteModal` sets/clears `createParent` and opens the modal. All 26 Notes store tests pass; `svelte-check` reports 0 errors.\n\n**Pre-existing issues noted (unrelated to this job):** 2 full-suite test failures — `TodoFilterService` week-filter test (month-boundary bug in the test itself, fails today 2026-09-05) and `logic-leaves` StatisticWidget color-class test — plus pre-existing lint noise (`fade` unused import, prettier drift) left untouched to keep the change minimal. All documented in `implementation.md`.","time":{"start":1788620136716,"end":1788620140346}}}
